{"name":"Trumpet Flower","hex":"#e49977","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"trumpet flower","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several species of flowering plants with trumpet-like flowers\nIncarvillea spp., native to central and eastern Asia (Chinese trumpet flower)\nCollomia spp.\nDatura meteloides, a perennial herb of the southwestern U.S. (desert trumpet flower)\nGelsemium sempervirens, native to North America (evening trumpetflower)\nOroxylum indicum, native to India (Indian trumpetflower)\nBeaumontia grandiflora (Nepal trumpet flower, Easter lily vine)\nSalpiglossis sinuata, native to Chile (velvet trumpet flower)\nDolichandrone atrovirens, native to India (wavy trumpet flower)\nTecoma stans (yellow bells, yellow trumpet flower, yellow elder)\nStereospermum chelonoides (syn. Bignonia suaveolens); fragrant padritree","Incarvillea spp., native to central and eastern Asia (Chinese trumpet flower)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trumpet_flower"}],"entries":[{"title":"Trumpetflower","blocks":[{"text":"Trumpetflower or trumpet flower may refer to several plants:"},{"items":["Chinese trumpet flower, Incarvillea, native to central and eastern Asia","Evening trumpetflower, Gelsemium sempervirens, native to North America","Indian trumpetflower, Oroxylum indicum, native to India","Velvet trumpet flower, Salpiglossis sinuata, native to Chile","Wavy trumpet flower, Dolichandrone atrovirens, native to India"]}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trumpetflower","wikidata":"Q7847821"},{"title":"Trumpet","blocks":[{"text":"The trumpet is a brass instrument. The most common type of trumpet is a transposing instrument in B♭, with pitches sounding a whole step lower than written. The trumpet family includes instruments ranging from the piccolo trumpet, with the highest register in the brass family, to the bass trumpet, pitched one octave below the standard B♭ or C trumpet."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Yamaha_Trumpet_YTR-8335LA_crop.jpg/330px-Yamaha_Trumpet_YTR-8335LA_crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trumpet","wikidata":"Q8338"},{"title":"Flower","blocks":[{"text":"Flowers, also known as blossoms and blooms, are the reproductive structures of flowering plants. Typically, they are structured in four circular levels around the end of a stalk. These include: sepals, which are modified leaves that support the flower; petals, often designed to attract pollinators; male stamens, where pollen is presented; and female gynoecia, where pollen is received and its movement is facilitated to the egg. When flowers are arranged in a group, they are known collectively as an inflorescence."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Magnolia_grandiflora_-_flower_1.jpg/330px-Magnolia_grandiflora_-_flower_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flower","wikidata":"Q506"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Musicians_at_the_coal_yard_-_DPLA_-_654d5920548ca26c571a5337d7807c60.jpg/500px-Musicians_at_the_coal_yard_-_DPLA_-_654d5920548ca26c571a5337d7807c60.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Musicians_at_the_coal_yard_-_DPLA_-_654d5920548ca26c571a5337d7807c60.jpg/500px-Musicians_at_the_coal_yard_-_DPLA_-_654d5920548ca26c571a5337d7807c60.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Trio of trumpeters in Toledo, Ohio, approximately 1940","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMusicians_at_the_coal_yard_-_DPLA_-_654d5920548ca26c571a5337d7807c60.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Trompette_d%27argent_et_sa_sourdine_en_bois_du_tombeau_de_Tout%C3%A2nkhamon_2.jpg/500px-T